        { "@type": "ListItem", position: 3, name: "Costco Treadmills", item: "https://www.treadmillreviewsusa.com/costco-treadmill/" },
      ],
    },
    {
      "@type": "FAQPage",
      mainEntity: [
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          name: "Are Costco treadmills good?",
          acceptedAnswer: {
            "@type": "Answer",
            text: "There is no Costco treadmill — Costco sells NordicTrack, ProForm, Sole, Horizon and others, and the answer depends entirely on which machine. The selection is curated and narrow, so the floor is higher than an open online marketplace and you are unlikely to end up with an unsupported brand. Judge the specific machine on its deck length, motor rating, capacity and warranty, not on the retailer.",
          },
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          name: "Can you return a treadmill to Costco?",
          acceptedAnswer: {
            "@type": "Answer",
            text: "Costco's return terms are generous by retail standards, but confirm the current policy for the specific item before buying, since large-item handling and category terms vary and change. The bigger constraint is practical: a treadmill is 150 to 300 lbs, partially assembled, in a room away from your front door. That effort is the real deductible, and it is high enough that many intended returns never happen.",
          },
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          name: "Is the Costco model the same as the one I read a review of?",
          acceptedAnswer: {
            "@type": "Answer",
            text: "Not necessarily. Large retailers frequently carry model variants with their own model numbers, and the differences can include console, deck, motor rating or warranty length. Write down the full model designation from the listing, find that exact string on the manufacturer's site, and compare deck dimensions, continuous-duty motor rating, weight capacity and warranty. Warranty is where the difference most often lives.",
          },
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          name: "Does Costco deliver and assemble treadmills?",
          acceptedAnswer: {
            "@type": "Answer",
            text: "It depends on the item and the arrangement, which is why you should ask before buying rather than after. Large-item delivery ranges from kerbside to room-of-choice with assembly and packaging removal, and those are very different services. Kerbside delivery of a boxed treadmill is a genuine two-person job, so either arrange help or price the delivery upgrade into the purchase.",
