        <!-- Closing CTA -->
        <div class="mt-16 bg-gray-900 text-white rounded-2xl p-8">
          <h2 class="text-2xl font-black text-white mb-4">The Bottom Line</h2>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            Costco is a good way to buy a treadmill you cannot evaluate in advance, because
            <strong class="text-white">a generous return window on a product that takes weeks to
            assess is genuinely valuable</strong> — and the curated selection means you are unlikely
            to end up with a machine nobody stocks parts for.
          </p>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            Two things decide whether it works out. Check the exact model number against the
            manufacturer's own specification, because retailer variants differ and the warranty is
            where it usually shows. And
            <a href="/best-time-of-year-to-buy-a-treadmill/" class="text-[#5AA9FF] font-bold no-underline">check the timing</a>
            — buying the right machine in the wrong month costs more than buying it at the wrong
            shop.
          </p>
